        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "The \"Stringing-Along Toy Theory\" compares \"threads\" to gravity wells, made of stretched spacetime strands that anchor to the big bang's central point. These strands stretch and distort as spacetime expands, maintaining a connection to the origin. They might tangle if there's rotational differential between the center and expanding surface. This idea parallels how minds connect through \"strands\" of language."
          ]
        },
